---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import evidence from '../../../../../public/equipment/14-01/verification.json';
import metrics from '../../../../../public/equipment/14-01/interactions.json';
const asset='/equipment/14-01/',doc='https://www.instron.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/5940-single-column-table-frames-system-support.pdf',grips='https://www.instron.com/en/products/testing-accessories/grips/screw-side-action-grips/',clemson='https://www.clemson.edu/centers-institutes/scbiocraft/bet/instruments.html';
const inputs=[['widthMm','Gauge width (mm)',.5,12,5],['thicknessMm','Gauge thickness (mm)',.05,3,1],['gaugeMm','Gauge length (mm)',5,50,25],['modulusGPa','Reference modulus (GPa)',.005,5,2],['strokeMm','Crosshead stroke (mm)',0,3,.1],['speedMmMin','Crosshead speed (mm/min)',.05,20,2],['frameNPerMm','Load-train stiffness (N/mm; 0 = rigid)',0,10000,0],['steps','Samples',5,301,51]];
const list=o=>typeof o==='string'?o:Object.entries(o).map(([k,v])=>k+': '+(typeof v==='number'?Number(v.toPrecision(8)):String(v))).join('; ');
---
<Layout pageTitle="Instron 5944 tension bench" subtitle="" description="Pull an inert virtual polymer coupon and inspect force, strain and load-cell range." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment" id="tensile"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/14-01/">← Equipment 14-01</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#tensile-verify">Verification</a></nav>
<header><p class="eq-meta">14-01 / Mechanical characterization / Virtual tensile test</p><h2>Instron 5944</h2><p>Pull a 5 × 1 mm ideal polymer gauge by 0.1 mm. The default run should read 40 N. Then try a 0.2 mm stroke and the virtual 50 N cell to see where the requested load exceeds the range.</p></header>
<div class="t-grid"><section class="t-card"><h3>01 · Inspect the load train</h3><div class="t-row" id="t-views">{['Bench','Front','Side','Grips','Rear'].map(n=><button data-view={n.toLowerCase()}>{n}</button>)}<button id="t-xr" disabled>VR unavailable</button></div>
<canvas id="t-model" aria-label="Orbitable Instron 5944 with clickable grips"></canvas><p id="t-asset" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p>Drag to orbit. Scroll or pinch to zoom. Click a grip to open or close it, the pendant to zero, or the monitor to run. The same actions are available on the form.</p></section>
<section class="t-card"><h3>02 · Mount and measure</h3><form id="t-config">
<div class="t-row">{[['upper','Upper grip'],['lower','Lower grip'],['load','Remove coupon'],['zero','Zero displacement']].map(([id,t])=><button type="button" id={'t-'+id}>{t}</button>)}</div>
<div class="t-fields"><label>Specimen ID<input name="sampleId" value="polymer-reference-01" maxlength="96" required /></label>
<label>Cell<select name="cellN"><option value="500">500 N</option><option value="50">50 N</option></select></label>
{inputs.map(([n,t,min,max,v])=><label>{t}<input name={n} type="number" min={min} max={max} value={v} step={n==='steps'?'1':'any'}/></label>)}</div>
<div class="t-row"><button class="t-run" id="t-run" type="submit">Run tensile test</button><button id="t-reset" type="button">Restore example</button></div></form>
<p id="t-status" role="status">Mounted, grips closed, displacement zeroed.</p></section></div>
<section class="t-card"><h3>03 · Force and strain</h3><p id="t-result" role="status">No measurement yet.</p><div class="t-grid"><svg id="t-force" viewBox="0 0 550 200" role="img" aria-label="Force versus crosshead displacement"></svg><svg id="t-stress" viewBox="0 0 550 200" role="img" aria-label="Engineering stress versus gauge strain"></svg></div>
<div class="t-row"><button id="t-json" disabled>Measurement JSON</button><button id="t-csv" disabled>Point CSV</button></div></section>
<section><h3>Frame and model</h3><div class="t-grid"><figure><img src={asset+'front.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original Instron frame rendering"/><figcaption>Original frame drawing. Compare <a href={doc+'#page=30'}>Fig. 2-1, Instron M10-16246-EN Rev E</a>.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={asset+'work.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original Instron virtual grip and coupon rendering"/><figcaption>Original simplified load string. Compare <a href={grips}>500 N 2710-112 screw-side-action grips</a> and <a href={clemson}>Clemson’s 5944 cell options</a>.</figcaption></figure></div>
<p>Selected 2 kN single-column Instrument with nominal frame W × H × D 459 × 1,383 × 614 mm (manual Table 2-5, pp. 2-11–12), 500 N side-action configuration and a selectable 50 N acquisition model. Load cell housing and jaw offsets are approximated. The visual and numerical coupon are original training geometry, not an ASTM specimen. Real instrument crosshead travel is 890 mm in this manual; this software only allows 0–3 mm for the example and does not control hardware.</p></section>
<section><h3>Numerical contract</h3><p>Gauge stiffness is EA/L. An optional finite frame stiffness K in series makes the measured slope 1/(L/EA + 1/K). Strain uses specimen extension F/(EA/L), not total crosshead motion; stress is F/A. The trace fits initial crosshead and modulus slopes through valid points up to 1% gauge strain. Above 2%, the model withholds force; above the selected load-cell limit it retains ideal demand but withholds measured force and stress. No grip slip, strain-rate dependence, yield, rupture or uncertainty model.</p>
<p>Exports have specimen ID, geometry, acquisition limits, sample and result revisions, each reading’s flags and SI units. <a href={asset+'output-schema.json'}>Output schema</a> · <a href={asset+'example-result.json'}>Example result</a>. These are simulated readings, not certification.</p></section>
<section id="tensile-verify"><h3>Verification</h3><div class="t-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Test</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Outcome</th></tr></thead><tbody>{evidence.map(x=><tr><td>{x.id}</td><td>{list(x.expected)}</td><td>{list(x.actual)}</td><td>{x.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p><a href={asset+'reference-plan.json'}>Predeclared cases and tolerances</a> · <a href={asset+'verification.json'}>Numerical evidence</a> · <a href={asset+'instron-5944.glb'} download>Meter GLB</a> · <a href={asset+'geometry-source.mjs'}>Editable geometry</a> · <a href={asset+'make-model.mjs'}>Generator</a> + <a href={asset+'mesh-writer.mjs'}>mesh writer</a> · <a href={asset+'interactions.json'}>Interaction anchors</a>. {metrics.triangles.toLocaleString()} triangles, {metrics.draws} material draws, {Math.round(metrics.bytes/1024)} KiB. Optional WebXR controller actions; physical headset untested.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/14-01/client.mjs';</script>
<style>
#tensile header{padding:1.3rem 0;max-width:72ch}#tensile h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,6vw,4rem);margin:.1rem 0}#tensile section{margin:1rem 0}.t-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.t-card{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem;min-width:0}.t-card h3{margin:.35rem 0}.t-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.35rem;margin:.5rem 0}.t-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.5rem}.t-fields label{display:grid;gap:.2rem}.t-fields input,.t-fields select,#tensile button{min-width:0;min-height:2.4rem;box-sizing:border-box;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:3px;font:inherit;background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);padding:.3rem .5rem}#tensile select option{background:var(--menuBg,Canvas);color:var(--text,CanvasText)}#tensile button:disabled{opacity:.55}.t-run{background:#47586d!important;color:white!important}#t-model{width:100%;height:clamp(300px,34vw,440px);display:block;background:#eeeae1;touch-action:none}#tensile svg{width:100%;max-height:11rem}#tensile figure{margin:0}#tensile img{width:100%;height:auto}#tensile table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.85rem}#tensile th,#tensile td{text-align:left;padding:.4rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}.t-scroll{overflow:auto}@media(max-width:820px){.t-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.t-fields{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}
</style>
